# Docker commands that I use:

To start conainers (data will be saved in volume):
`docker-compose up`

To list active conainers:
`docker ps`

After listing active containers to enter the container run:
`docker exec -it <container_name> sh` to enter container shell
`docker exec -it <container_name> ...` after which we car run commands like ls
`docker exec -it <container_name> ls /var/www/html/vendor`

To start and build containers:
`docker-compose up --build`

To remove containers and volumes:
`docker-compose down -v`

To remove volumes (don't think I will be using this):
`docker volume rm <your-project-name>_db_data`

## DB related commands:

To enter db container and execute mysql command (`SHOW TABLES;`):
`docker-compose exec db mysql -u myuser -pmypassword myapp_db`

To enter db and list sql scipt placed in entry point:
`docker-compose exec db ls /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/`

#### Enter the (MySQL) container:

`docker-compose exec db bash`

#### Access the MySQL CLI:

`mysql -u myuser -pmypassword myapp_db`

#### Manually run the SQL script:

`SOURCE /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/db_ini.sql;`

When entering the container using `docker-compose exec ...` is the same as `docker exec ...`
the difference is that for the first we write the container name as it is in docker-compose file
and for the second we have to check container name with `docker ps` command

// return all records
GET /person

// return a specific record
GET /person/{id}

// create a new record
POST /person

// update an existing record
PUT /person/{id}

// delete an existing record
DELETE /person/{id}

To run PHP server
php -S 127.0.0.1:8000 -t public

#### New db credentials

DB_HOST=db
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=myapp_db
DB_USERNAME=myuser
DB_PASSWORD=mypassword

#### Old db credentials

DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=api_example
DB_USERNAME=api_user
DB_PASSWORD=api_password

I removed from FE http://127.0.0.1:8000/user?action=register
To get register we did
$action = $\_GET['action'] ?? ''; // Fetch action from query params

Now we are accessing this API by http://127.0.0.1:8000/user/register

You will possiby need to run these two commands
composer require vlucas/phpdotenv
composer require firebase/php-jwt

There will be a SQL script to initialize the database and to create tables.
